From 1e4e4bab0ca81e9a38b5605ba1d1ac8d8ba6e1be Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: luoxiaoyu <137460387@qq.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 10:29:24 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] Writing a stick: verify the recovery image before erasing,
 and hash the preflight sample

A local BaseSystem.dmg was checked chunk by chunk only while it was copied, which happens after the
stick is erased. A damaged, unsigned or wrong-version local image cost the user their stick before
the refusal. The online preflight read a small range and only counted the bytes, so any server
could pass it with bytes that were not Apple's.

- apple.verify_local(): signed chunklist, exact size and every chunk's sha256, run from cli_write
  before write() is called; the stick is untouched on failure.
- local_image(folder, darwin) reads an optional BaseSystem.product.json {product, darwin} and refuses
  an image recorded for another macOS. Without it, the writer prints that the version is unrecorded.
- preflight() samples the whole first chunk (up to 64 MiB) and checks its signed sha256.
- copy_local() survives a stick remount per chunk and fsyncs image and chunklist; download() fsyncs too.
- Regression tests: no erase on a bad local image, version marker, preflight hash match/mismatch.
